notes               = "Untitled in source. The source gives a decade, not a year — دههٔ ۷۰, the 1370s (1991–2001) — and it is listed as printed rather than pinned to a year. The first verb is the point: سرودن is what you do to a poem, not a painting, so 'I sing my paintings' is the poet-painter's whole position in four words (and Farrokhi's thesis in the introduction). قصه ('tale') and غصه ('grief') differ by one dot in Persian and arrive as a near-echo; the lantern reaches for it with tale / tally. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

نقاشی‌هایم را می‌سرایم...
نه بوم می‌خواهد،
نَه... دیوار...
نَه قصهٔ خریدار
نَه غصه، کُنجِ انبار...
دههٔ ۷۰

===machine===

I compose my paintings...
It wants no canvas,
no... wall...
no tale of a buyer
no grief in the corner of a storeroom...
The 1370s

===lantern===

I sing my paintings...
It wants no canvas,
no... wall...
no tale of a buyer,
no tally of grief in a store-room corner...

The 1370s

